    "created_at": "2020-02-09T12:40:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-02-09T12:40:30Z",
    "body": "> What do we want to be shown before a lazy-loaded image is loaded? (I assume same as normal images -- hide the alt)\r\n\r\nI agree, hide the alt. I think per the lazy load spec, this is clear right? Since the #updating-the-image-data algorithm is suspended, from the perspective of rendering the image, it is just like the image is taking a long time to load?",
